// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 282: Conditional processing (compile if) (page 375)
action new_flow {
    activity { ... }
  }
When the false case is triggered, the code in Example 282 is equivalent to:
action old_flow {
    activity { ... }
  }
23.3 compile has
compile has allows conditional elaboration to reason about the existence of types and constants. The
compile has expression evaluates to true if a type or constant has been previously declared unconditionally
or within an enabled conditional block (see 23.1.2); otherwise, it evaluates to false.
